## Installation

### Requirements
- Python 3.8+ (added to system PATH)
- Windows 10 / 11
- Administrator account

### Steps
1. Put all 4 files in the same folder
2. Right-click `install.py` → **Run as administrator**
3. Enter how many days to stay locked (e.g. `30`)
4. Confirm → done

---

## How the Protection Works

```
Every 30 seconds (Windows Service):
  ├─ Re-writes hosts file (sites + NSFW reddit + DoH domains)
  ├─ Flushes DNS cache
  └─ Kills any blocked processes (apps)

Every 5 minutes (Windows Service):
  ├─ Re-applies DoH-disable registry keys (Chrome/Edge/Firefox/Brave)
  ├─ Re-applies Safe Search registry keys
  └─ Re-applies keyword filter registry keys

Every 5 minutes (Task Scheduler Watchdog):
  ├─ If blocker_service.py was deleted → restores from base64 backup
  ├─ If service was stopped → restarts it
  ├─ If hosts block is missing → re-applies it
  └─ Re-applies all registry policies
```

---

## Attack Resistance

| Attack | Result |
|---|---|
| Delete `blocker_service.py` | Watchdog restores it within 5 min |
| Stop the Windows service | Watchdog restarts it within 5 min |
| Manually edit hosts file | Service re-writes it within 30 sec |
| Delete registry keys | Service re-writes them within 5 min |
| Use DNS-over-HTTPS in browser | Registry policy disables DoH; DoH domains blocked in hosts |
| Open a blocked app | Process killed within 30 sec |
| Run `uninstall.py` early | Rejected — shows remaining lock time |

